      "type": "text",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Cache-Control directives determine whether a stored response can be reused, for how long, and under which constraints.",
          "bullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "An expired response can still be revalidated with the origin using a validator such as ETag.",
          "bullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "A successful If-None-Match request returns 304 Not Modified, retaining the stored representation while refreshing its metadata.",
          "bullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "no-cache permits reuse after validation, whereas no-store forbids retaining the response.",
          "bullet": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Freshness directives govern reuse, while validators provide a separate path for checking whether an expired response remains current. Emphasize that no-cache requires validation but no-store prevents storage altogether."
}

